  Deliberately migration-TRIGGERING channel export. Its channel root is versioned
  schema 3.4.0 - chosen at or above schema 3.0.0 so the explicit version attribute
  keeps it clear of the ImportConverter3_0_0 NPE boundary (18-08 Decision 4), and
  below schema 3.5.0 so Channel.migrate3_5_0(), the exact v26.6.0 rollback seam
  (commit 22940c0f8, partially reverted in 6a483ab9d), runs on EVERY harness import.
  It is derived from legacy-migration-test.xml (the schema 3.6.0 fixture, id
  00000011-0000-0000-0000-000000000011) with only the <channel> root version changed,
  the id/name changed to fit the smoke-harness's 12-channel numbering, the trailing
  exportData block removed, and the pre-migration channel-level elements
  (enabled/lastModified/codeTemplateLibraries) and properties-level archiveEnabled
  restored so migrate3_5_0() has real content to consume.

  Every nested version attribute (sourceConnector, transformer, filter, properties,
  etc.) deliberately stays at schema 3.6.0. Rationale, verified in source:
  Transformer.migrate3_5_0() calls element.removeChild("steps").getChildElements()
  and Filter.migrate3_5_0() calls element.removeChild("rules").getChildElements();
  this fixture's transformer/filter bodies are post-3.5 shaped (<elements/>), so
  downgrading THEIR version attributes would NPE inside
  MigratableConverter.migrateElement() and break the fixture even on healthy
  xstream. The channel-root migration alone drives the exact
  Channel.migrate3_5_0() DOM-mutation-then-reload sequence the regression broke.

  This fixture must NEVER be version-rewritten to the current schema version.
  run-smoke-test.sh's substitute_fixtures() excludes both legacy-migration-*
  fixtures from its version-rewrite sed and its envsubst pass for exactly this
  reason - rewriting either one would silently re-open the NET-05 break-proof
  hole this fixture pair exists to close (NET-05/SC-4, D-13/D-14, plan 18-10).
  NEVER "fix" this file's schema version 3.4.0 channel-root attribute, and NEVER
  add back an exportData block (migrate3_5_0() would then create a duplicate
  exportData child and fail deserialization on healthy xstream).
-->
